Hi  Philipp,

The first two warning messages are from raster and not from ctmm. I'm actually not familiar with them, but they don't sound good.

For running rsf.fit(), the area only needs to go a bit beyond the home range to be valid. Using a larger area will only slow that part down. The fitted model can then be used to run suitability on different sized rasters from what was used in the fitting. I don't think this will fix the issue though.

If you can't figure out the raster issue, you can create a minimal working example (MWE) in a shared folder for me and I can take a look at it.

Best,
Chris

